Article 17
(1) Women's empowerment in the field of Education as referred to in Article 12 paragraph (3) letter e, shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus with authority over education, individuals, communities, the education sector and the business sector.
(2) Women's Empowerment in the field of education as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented through:
a. provision of formal, nonformal and informal education for women;
b. provision of formal education for compulsory education of a minimum of 12 (twelve) years for women shall be implemented by government and private institutions;
c. nonformal education aimed at improving the abilities and skills of women shall be conducted through equivalency education package A, Package B and Package C as well as courses/training;
d. women who become victims of violence shall have their rights protected to obtain continuity of education both online and offline in formal schools, or through nonformal pathways/equivalency education;
e. in the context of strengthening women's capacity in the field of education, every education provider shall facilitate the continuity of education for female students.

